SQLite bundled source provenance
================================

This directory contains the SQLite amalgamation bundled by QElectroTech for
builds that enable QET_USE_BUNDLED_SQLITE3.

Upstream project:
  https://sqlite.org/
  Release: 3.53.4
  Fossil check-in: bf7c7f30031888f4e796e429ab3978879485
  Source ID: 2026-07-24 19:02:57
    bf7c7f30031888f4e796e429ab3978879485813aaca6f641c7b33e4e09459bcc

The bundled SQLite source consists of:

  include/sqlite3.h
  src/sqlite3.c

These files are the SQLite amalgamation: generated source combining the
SQLite core and its public C API header into a form that can be compiled as a
single translation unit. The files identify SQLite version 3.53.4 and the
Fossil check-in listed above in their upstream headers.

SQLite is released into the public domain. See the notices in the bundled
SQLite files and the SQLite copyright page for the applicable dedication and
license information:

  https://sqlite.org/copyright.html

The following file was added by QElectroTech and is not part of SQLite:

  CMakeLists.txt

It provides the local static-library target and include-path setup needed to
build the bundled amalgamation. It is covered by the QElectroTech license
notice in that file and is not part of the SQLite public-domain source.
